&lt;p&gt;The parse is bounded — 4 MiB per cell, a nesting depth of 1000 — so a
notebook from anyone cannot make it run long or exhaust memory; a cell over
the limits fails with a message saying so.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Names.&lt;/strong&gt; A Julia cell joins the &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/cells/"&gt;rules of cells&lt;/a&gt; and the
dependency graph: one definition per name, no assignment to another cell&amp;rsquo;s
variable, a name starting with &lt;code&gt;_&lt;/code&gt; kept in its cell. Its names follow Julia&amp;rsquo;s
own scope rules for an interactive context, as written in
&lt;a href="https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/manual/variables-and-scoping/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Scope of Variables&lt;/a&gt;
(Julia manual, 1.12):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Construct&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the notebook&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x = 1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;a, b = …&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x::Int = 1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;global x = 1&lt;/code&gt; at the top level, or in &lt;code&gt;if&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;begin&lt;/code&gt; there&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines the variable&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;f(x) = …&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;function f … end&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;macro m … end&lt;/code&gt; (as &lt;code&gt;@m&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines a function or macro&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;const C = …&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;struct S&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;abstract type&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;primitive type&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;module M&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines a constant or type&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;using A&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;using A: x, y&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;import A.B&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;import A as B&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines what it binds (&lt;code&gt;A&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;B&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;function&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;macro&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;struct&lt;/code&gt; bodies, &lt;code&gt;let&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;do&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, comprehensions and generators&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;hard scopes: an assignment there makes a local&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;for&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;while&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;try&lt;/code&gt; at the top level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;soft scopes: an assignment there to an existing global assigns it (as in the REPL and IJulia); otherwise it makes a local of the loop&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a name read before the cell assigns it, in any scope where no local binds it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a use: the cell depends on the cell that defines it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These rules are checked against julia itself: 61 cells, from each kind of
definition to keyword defaults, &lt;code&gt;where&lt;/code&gt; bounds and nested generators, are
lowered by julia 1.12.6 (through &lt;code&gt;REPL.softscope&lt;/code&gt;, the soft-scope rule of the
REPL), and the globals julia declares and reads are the names go-notebook
finds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Across languages.&lt;/strong&gt; A Julia cell&amp;rsquo;s variables are seen by Go and Ruby cells,
and a Julia cell sees theirs, as between Ruby and Go (see
&lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/ruby/"&gt;Ruby cells&lt;/a&gt;); functions, macros, constants and types stay in Julia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-does-not-work-yet-running"&gt;What does not work yet: running&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-does-not-work-yet-running"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-does-not-work-yet-running" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Running a Julia cell fails, clearly, and the cells that need it say why:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```julia
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
