&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-console" data-lang="console"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="gp"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; notebook run julia.md
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 0 (line 4, ran in 11µs)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 1 (line 8, not run)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; error: Julia cells are parsed and checked, but not run yet: execution arrives with go-embedded-julia&amp;#39;s runtime (milestone M3)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 2 (line 13, not run)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; error: blocked: it depends on cell 1, a Julia cell, and Julia cells are not run yet
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 3 (line 17, ran in 28µs)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; 20
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;notebook: 2 cell(s) failed
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(Real transcripts, from go-notebook&amp;rsquo;s main branch on an Apple M4 Max.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a Julia cell never runs, and &lt;code&gt;notebook run&lt;/code&gt; exits non-zero;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;every cell that reads what a Julia cell defines — directly or through other
cells, in any language — is &lt;strong&gt;blocked&lt;/strong&gt;, not silently skipped;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the other cells run as usual.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;go-notebook starts no external &lt;code&gt;julia&lt;/code&gt;: the cells will run on
go-embedded-julia&amp;rsquo;s own runtime, in the same worker as Go and Ruby cells,
when it exists. The HTML page shows a Julia cell&amp;rsquo;s source uncoloured (go-rouge
has no Julia lexer yet).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="in-the-browser"&gt;In the browser&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="in-the-browser"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#in-the-browser" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/playground/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;playground&lt;/a&gt; parses and checks
Julia cells in the same way, in WebAssembly: a syntax error is shown at its
line, the cell&amp;rsquo;s badge reads &lt;strong&gt;Julia — not runnable yet&lt;/strong&gt;, and the cells that
read it are blocked. A Julia cell that parses is shown as &lt;em&gt;not run&lt;/em&gt;, and a cell
that reads it as &lt;em&gt;blocked&lt;/em&gt;, in the page&amp;rsquo;s neutral style and not as failures
(the playground&amp;rsquo;s results carry a typed &lt;code&gt;status&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;notrun&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;blocked&lt;/code&gt;, and
its site build accepts exactly those two for a Julia example, while a syntax
error still fails it).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Try it: the &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/playground/#4-julia" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Julia example notebook&lt;/a&gt;
has a Julia cell, a Go cell blocked on it and a Go cell that runs alone, and its
prose says that Julia cells are checked, not run, until
&lt;a href="https://go-embedded-julia.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-embedded-julia&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s runtime lands.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>